-- tests.l4 — tests for the encoding of the Diplomatic Appointments (Selection
-- Process) Bill 2026 (Cth). Every fact pattern is taken from the Bill's own
-- words; the section each test exercises is named beside it. Tests marked
-- "ISSUE n" pin down behaviour that ISSUES.md reports as a problem with the
-- Bill: they pass because the encoding reproduces what the Bill says, not
-- because the result is sensible.
--
-- Run from this folder:  l4 run tests.l4

IMPORT support
IMPORT definitions
IMPORT `selection-process`
IMPORT miscellaneous

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `the name`  IS A STRING
      ms          IS A LIST OF `Period of membership`
      mops        IS A LIST OF `Engagement under the MOP(S) Act`
      states      IS A LIST OF `Engagement as State or Territory political staff`
      roles       IS A LIST OF `Role with a political party`
GIVETH A `Person`
`a person called` `the name` `with` ms mops states roles MEANS `Person` WITH
    `name`                                              IS `the name`
    `periods of membership of a legislature`            IS ms
    `engagements under the MOP(S) Act`                  IS mops
    `engagements as State or Territory political staff` IS states
    `roles with political parties`                      IS roles

GIVEN `the name` IS A STRING
      ms         IS A LIST OF `Period of membership`
GIVETH A `Person`
`a former member called` `the name` `with` ms MEANS
    `a person called` `the name` `with` ms EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN l  IS A `Legislature`
      b  IS A `Calendar date`
      e  IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Period of membership`
`a membership of` l `from` b `to` e MEANS
    `Period of membership` WITH `legislature` IS l, `began` IS b, `ended` IS JUST e

`the test day` MEANS `the date` 2028 6 1
`Avery` MEANS `a person with no political history`

-- A senator 2010-07-01 to 2016-06-30: left the Senate more than 10 years
-- before the test day.
`Blake` MEANS `a former member called` "Blake" `with` (LIST `a membership of` `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` `from` (`the date` 2010 7 1) `to` (`the date` 2016 6 30))

-- A State MP 2011-03-26 to 2019-03-23: left within the last 10 years.
`Casey` MEANS `a former member called` "Casey" `with` (LIST `a membership of` `the Parliament of a State` `from` (`the date` 2011 3 26) `to` (`the date` 2019 3 23))

-- Membership ending exactly on, and the day before, the first day of the
-- 10-year window that ends on the test day (2018-06-01).
`Ellis` MEANS `a former member called` "Ellis" `with` (LIST `a membership of` `the legislature of a Territory` `from` (`the date` 2012 10 20) `to` (`the date` 2018 6 1))
`Finley` MEANS `a former member called` "Finley" `with` (LIST `a membership of` `the legislature of a Territory` `from` (`the date` 2012 10 20) `to` (`the date` 2018 5 31))

-- A sitting member.
`Gray` MEANS `a former member called` "Gray" `with` (LIST `Period of membership` WITH `legislature` IS `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`, `began` IS `the date` 2022 5 21, `ended` IS NOTHING)

-- A member whose term begins after the test day.
`Harper` MEANS `a former member called` "Harper" `with` (LIST `Period of membership` WITH `legislature` IS `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`, `began` IS `the date` 2028 7 1, `ended` IS NOTHING)

-- Staff and party history.
`Drew` MEANS `a person called` "Drew" `with` EMPTY (LIST `Engagement under the MOP(S) Act` WITH `the position occupied by the employer` IS `a Minister (including the Prime Minister)`) EMPTY EMPTY
`Jordan` MEANS `a person called` "Jordan" `with` EMPTY (LIST `Engagement under the MOP(S) Act` WITH `the position occupied by the employer` IS `a shadow Minister`) EMPTY EMPTY
`Kendall` MEANS `a person called` "Kendall" `with` EMPTY (LIST `Engagement under the MOP(S) Act` WITH `the position occupied by the employer` IS `some other position`) EMPTY EMPTY
`Logan` MEANS `a person called` "Logan" `with` EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `Engagement as State or Territory political staff` WITH `employed under a law of a State or Territory` IS TRUE, `the employer's position is equivalent or corresponds to one in (b)(i) to (vi)` IS TRUE) EMPTY
`Morgan` MEANS `a person called` "Morgan" `with` EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `Engagement as State or Territory political staff` WITH `employed under a law of a State or Territory` IS FALSE, `the employer's position is equivalent or corresponds to one in (b)(i) to (vi)` IS TRUE) EMPTY
`Quinn` MEANS `a person called` "Quinn" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `Role with a political party` WITH `capacity` IS `an officer`, `the party is registered under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918` IS TRUE)
`Reese` MEANS `a person called` "Reese" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `Role with a political party` WITH `capacity` IS `an employee`, `the party is registered under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918` IS TRUE)
`Sage` MEANS `a person called` "Sage" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `Role with a political party` WITH `capacity` IS `a member only`, `the party is registered under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918` IS TRUE)
`Taylor` MEANS `a person called` "Taylor" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (LIST `Role with a political party` WITH `capacity` IS `an officer`, `the party is registered under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918` IS FALSE)
`Uma` MEANS `a person called` "Uma" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
`Vic` MEANS `a person called` "Vic" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
`Wren` MEANS `a person called` "Wren" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
`Yael` MEANS `a person called` "Yael" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
`Zane` MEANS `a person called` "Zane" `with` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A `Proposed candidate`
`plainly` p MEANS `Proposed candidate` WITH `the person` IS p, `reasons are set out despite a significant political affiliation` IS FALSE

GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A `Proposed candidate`
`with reasons` p MEANS `Proposed candidate` WITH `the person` IS p, `reasons are set out despite a significant political affiliation` IS TRUE

GIVEN d  IS A `Calendar date`
      cs IS A LIST OF `Proposed candidate`
GIVETH A `Candidate list`
`a list given on` d `proposing` cs MEANS `Candidate list` WITH `given on` IS d, `the proposed candidates` IS cs

GIVEN d IS A `Calendar date`
      n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Written notice`
`a notice on` d `recommending` n MEANS `Written notice` WITH `given on` IS d, `the decision` IS `recommending the appointment of` n

GIVEN d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Written notice`
`a referral notice on` d MEANS `Written notice` WITH `given on` IS d, `the decision` IS `referring the matter back to the Minister`

GIVEN est      IS A `Calendar date`
      second   IS A BOOLEAN
      l        IS A MAYBE `Candidate list`
      notice   IS A MAYBE `Written notice`
GIVETH A `Selection Committee`
`a Committee established on` est second l notice MEANS `Selection Committee` WITH
    `established on`                 IS est
    `the members`                    IS LIST "Member 1", "Member 2", "Member 3"
    `second or subsequent Committee` IS second
    `the candidate list`             IS l
    `the written notice`             IS notice

`the day of Royal Assent` MEANS `the date` 2026 12 1

§ `s 8 — Political affiliations`

-- s 8(1): a past member who left within the last 10 years.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `Casey` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `Casey` `on` `the test day` EQUALS `a disqualifying political affiliation`
-- s 8(1): a sitting member ("is ... a member").
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `Gray` `on` `the test day`
-- s 8(1) / 8(2)(a): a member who left more than 10 years ago.
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `Blake` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `Blake` `on` `the test day` EQUALS `a significant political affiliation (and no disqualifying one)`
-- The 10-year boundary (ISSUE 4: the encoding includes the first day of the window).
#ASSERT `s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `Ellis` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(1) — has a disqualifying political affiliation` `Finley` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Finley` `on` `the test day`
-- The same person changes category as time passes (ISSUE 4).
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `Casey` `on` (`the date` 2029 3 24) EQUALS `a significant political affiliation (and no disqualifying one)`
-- A membership that has not yet begun is not "is, or has been".
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `Harper` `on` `the test day` EQUALS `neither`
-- Every past member falls under s 8(1) or s 8(2)(a): there is no gap between them.
#ASSERT NOT `the political affiliation of` `Blake` `on` (`the date` 2017 1 1) EQUALS `neither`
#ASSERT NOT `the political affiliation of` `Finley` `on` (`the date` 2040 1 1) EQUALS `neither`
-- s 8(2)(b): staff of a Minister, of a shadow Minister; not of a backbencher.
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `Drew` `on` `the test day` EQUALS `a significant political affiliation (and no disqualifying one)`
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Jordan` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT `the political affiliation of` `Kendall` `on` `the test day` EQUALS `neither`
-- s 8(2)(c): State staff, only if employed "under a law of a State or Territory" (ISSUE 8).
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Logan` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Morgan` `on` `the test day`
-- s 8(2)(d): officer or employee of a registered party; not a mere member;
-- not an officer of a party registered only under State law (ISSUE 10).
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Quinn` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Reese` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Sage` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Taylor` `on` `the test day`
-- s 8(2)(b)-(d) have no time limit: staff work 40 years ago still counts.
#ASSERT `s 8(2) — has a significant political affiliation` `Drew` `on` (`the date` 2068 1 1)

§ `s 7 — Designated diplomatic offices`

#ASSERT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` `High Commissioner to the United Kingdom`
#ASSERT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`Ambassador and Permanent Representative to the United Nations` "Geneva")
#ASSERT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`another office of the Commonwealth` "Ambassador to France" TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`another office of the Commonwealth` "Ambassador to France" TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 7 — is a designated diplomatic office` (`another office of the Commonwealth` "a domestic office" FALSE TRUE)

§ `s 10 — The Minister's list`

`Committee 1` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING
`Committee 1, second or subsequent` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING
`day 5` MEANS `the date` 2028 1 15
`four with one significant, reasons given` MEANS `a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `with reasons` `Blake`, `plainly` `Uma`, `plainly` `Vic`)

-- s 10(1),(2): 4 candidates, 1 with a significant affiliation and reasons.
#ASSERT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` `four with one significant, reasons given`
-- s 10(2)(b): 2 significant among 4 is too many.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `with reasons` `Blake`, `with reasons` `Drew`, `plainly` `Uma`))
-- s 10(2)(c): 2 significant among 5 is allowed; 3 among 6 is not.
#ASSERT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `with reasons` `Blake`, `with reasons` `Drew`, `plainly` `Uma`, `plainly` `Vic`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `with reasons` `Blake`, `with reasons` `Drew`, `with reasons` `Quinn`, `plainly` `Uma`, `plainly` `Vic`))
-- s 10(2)(a): a candidate with a disqualifying affiliation.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Casey`, `plainly` `Uma`))
-- s 10(2)(d): no reasons for the significant candidate.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Blake`, `plainly` `Uma`))
-- s 10(1): fewer than 2, more than 10.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Uma`, `plainly` `Vic`, `plainly` `Wren`, `plainly` `Yael`, `plainly` `Zane`, `plainly` `Kendall`, `plainly` `Sage`, `plainly` `Taylor`, `plainly` `Morgan`, `plainly` `Harper`))
#ASSERT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Uma`, `plainly` `Vic`, `plainly` `Wren`, `plainly` `Yael`, `plainly` `Zane`, `plainly` `Kendall`, `plainly` `Sage`, `plainly` `Taylor`, `plainly` `Morgan`))
-- s 10(1): within 7 days of establishing the Committee (day 7 yes, day 8 no).
#ASSERT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` (`the date` 2028 1 17) `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Uma`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1` (`a list given on` (`the date` 2028 1 18) `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Uma`))
-- s 10(6): a second or subsequent Committee gets 2 or 3 candidates.
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1, second or subsequent` `four with one significant, reasons given`
#ASSERT `s 10(1),(2) — the list complies` `Committee 1, second or subsequent` (`a list given on` `day 5` `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `with reasons` `Blake`, `plainly` `Uma`))
-- s 10(3): two calendar months after the list (AIA s 2G), including into a leap February.
#ASSERT (`s 10(3) — the last day for the Committee's written notice` `four with one significant, reasons given`) `is the same day as` (`the date` 2028 3 15)
#ASSERT (`s 10(3) — the last day for the Committee's written notice` (`a list given on` (`the date` 2027 12 31) `proposing` EMPTY)) `is the same day as` (`the date` 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `s 10(3) — the Committee gave its written notice in time` (`a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE (JUST `four with one significant, reasons given`) (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 15))))
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(3) — the Committee gave its written notice in time` (`a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE (JUST `four with one significant, reasons given`) (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 16))))

§ `ss 12, 13 — Committees and their meetings`

-- s 12(3).
#ASSERT `s 12(3) — the Committee consists of 3 members` `Committee 1`
-- s 12(8), s 10(5): while Committee 1 has given no notice it is not dissolved,
-- and no second Committee may be established (ISSUE 11).
#ASSERT NOT `s 12(8) — the Minister may establish a Selection Committee, given` (LIST `Committee 1`) `on` (`the date` 2029 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 12(8) — the Minister may establish a Selection Committee, given` (LIST `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 1)))) `on` (`the date` 2028 3 2)
-- s 13: quorum of all 3; majority of the votes of the members.
#ASSERT `s 13 — the outcome of` (`Meeting` WITH `the number of members present` IS 3, `the votes` IS LIST `a vote for` "Avery", `a vote for` "Avery", `a vote for` "Uma") EQUALS `the Committee decides` (`recommending the appointment of` "Avery")
#ASSERT `s 13 — the outcome of` (`Meeting` WITH `the number of members present` IS 3, `the votes` IS LIST `a vote for` "Avery", `a vote for` "Uma", `a vote for` "Vic") EQUALS `the Committee decides` `referring the matter back to the Minister`
#ASSERT `s 13 — the outcome of` (`Meeting` WITH `the number of members present` IS 2, `the votes` IS LIST `a vote for` "Avery", `a vote for` "Avery") EQUALS `no decision: the meeting is not quorate`
-- ISSUE 12: one vote cast, two members not voting.
#ASSERT `s 13 — the outcome of` (`Meeting` WITH `the number of members present` IS 3, `the votes` IS LIST `a vote for` "Avery", `no vote`, `no vote`) EQUALS `the Committee decides` `referring the matter back to the Minister`

§ `s 9 — Appointments`

GIVEN appointee IS A `Person`
      made       IS A `Calendar date`
      cs         IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      earlier    IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
      satisfied  IS A BOOLEAN
      resolution IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appointment case`
`an appointment to Japan of` appointee `on` made cs earlier satisfied resolution MEANS `Appointment case` WITH
    `the office`                                     IS `Ambassador to Japan`
    `the appointee`                                  IS appointee
    `the day the appointment is made`                IS made
    `the day the term of the appointment starts`     IS made `plus calendar months` 1
    `the Selection Committees established for an appointment to the office` IS cs
    `the days of earlier appointments to the office` IS earlier
    `the Minister is satisfied the appointee does not have a significant political affiliation` IS satisfied
    `both Houses have passed a resolution approving the appointment` IS resolution

`Committee 1 recommends Avery` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE (JUST `four with one significant, reasons given`) (JUST (`a notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 1) `recommending` "Avery"))
`Committee 1 refers back` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE (JUST `four with one significant, reasons given`) (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 1)))
`Committee 2 refers back` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 3 10) TRUE (JUST (`a list given on` (`the date` 2028 3 12) `proposing` (LIST `plainly` `Avery`, `plainly` `Uma`))) (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2028 5 1)))
`Committee 1 recommends Casey` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE (JUST `four with one significant, reasons given`) (JUST (`a notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 1) `recommending` "Casey"))
`Committee 1 recommends Drew, who is not on its list` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2028 1 10) FALSE (JUST `four with one significant, reasons given`) (JUST (`a notice on` (`the date` 2028 3 1) `recommending` "Drew"))

-- s 9(2): appointment of the recommended person.
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Avery` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`) (LIST `the date` 2024 2 1) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `s 9(2) — on a Selection Committee's recommendation`
#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Avery` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`) EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `the appointment may be made on a Selection Committee's recommendation (s 9(2))`
-- s 9(2): someone else may not be appointed instead (no route).
#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Uma` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`) EMPTY TRUE TRUE) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `the appointment must not be made (s 14(1)); if made it is valid (s 14(2)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(3))`
-- ISSUE 1: the recommended person need not be appointed; nothing in the Bill
-- obliges it. Not appointing Avery is not a breach the encoding can see, and
-- the recommendation blocks s 9(3) for the vacancy.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(3) applies to` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Uma` `on` (`the date` 2028 9 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`, `Committee 2 refers back`, `Committee 2 refers back`) EMPTY TRUE TRUE)
-- s 10(7): a recommendation is spent once an appointment to the office is made.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) applies to` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Avery` `on` (`the date` 2028 9 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`) (LIST `the date` 2028 4 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- s 9(1)(a): recommended, but with a disqualifying affiliation.
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Casey` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Casey`) EMPTY TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `no route under section 9`
-- s 9(3): two referrals, then (c)(i) the Minister is satisfied / (c)(ii) both Houses.
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Avery` `on` (`the date` 2028 6 1) (LIST `Committee 1 refers back`, `Committee 2 refers back`) EMPTY TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `s 9(3)(c)(i) — after two referrals, the Minister being satisfied`
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Blake` `on` (`the date` 2028 6 1) (LIST `Committee 1 refers back`, `Committee 2 refers back`) EMPTY FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `s 9(3)(c)(ii) — after two referrals, with the approval of both Houses`
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Blake` `on` (`the date` 2028 6 1) (LIST `Committee 1 refers back`, `Committee 2 refers back`) EMPTY FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no route under section 9`
-- s 9(3)(b): one referral is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Avery` `on` (`the date` 2028 6 1) (LIST `Committee 1 refers back`) EMPTY TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `no route under section 9`
-- s 9(3) with both Houses' approval cannot rescue a disqualifying affiliation.
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Casey` `on` (`the date` 2028 6 1) (LIST `Committee 1 refers back`, `Committee 2 refers back`) EMPTY FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `no route under section 9`
-- ISSUE 2: a Committee recommends a person who was never on the Minister's
-- list (and who has a significant affiliation, the list's one such slot being
-- already used). s 9(2) is satisfied; only the broad reading of s 14(1) objects.
#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Drew` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Drew, who is not on its list`) EMPTY FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `s 9(2) — on a Selection Committee's recommendation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 14(1) — broad reading: the appointment is in accordance with this Act` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Drew` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Drew, who is not on its list`) EMPTY FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 14(1) — broad reading: the appointment is in accordance with this Act` (`an appointment to Japan of` `Avery` `on` (`the date` 2028 4 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`) EMPTY FALSE FALSE)

§ `ISSUE 3 — s 9(3) is not confined to the current vacancy`

-- (a) An earlier vacancy was filled on a recommendation in 2028. For the next
-- vacancy, two Committees refer the matter back in 2031. Read literally,
-- s 9(3)(a) fails forever, because a recommendation "has been made".
`2031 Committee A refers back` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2031 1 10) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2031 3 1)))
`2031 Committee B refers back` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the date` 2031 3 10) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (`a referral notice on` (`the date` 2031 5 1)))
`the second vacancy, after an earlier recommended appointment` MEANS `an appointment to Japan of` `Uma` `on` (`the date` 2031 7 1) (LIST `Committee 1 recommends Avery`, `2031 Committee A refers back`, `2031 Committee B refers back`) (LIST `the date` 2028 4 1) TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `s 9(3) applies to` `the second vacancy, after an earlier recommended appointment`
#ASSERT `s 9(3) applies to, vacancy-scoped reading` `the second vacancy, after an earlier recommended appointment`

-- (b) An earlier vacancy was filled under s 9(3) in 2028 after two referrals.
-- For the next vacancy in 2031 no Committee is established at all. Read
-- literally, the 2028 referrals still count, so s 9(3) is open at once.
`the second vacancy, with no Committee of its own` MEANS `an appointment to Japan of` `Uma` `on` (`the date` 2031 7 1) (LIST `Committee 1 refers back`, `Committee 2 refers back`) (LIST `the date` 2028 6 1) TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `s 9 — the route by which the appointment may be made` `the second vacancy, with no Committee of its own` EQUALS `s 9(3)(c)(i) — after two referrals, the Minister being satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(3) applies to, vacancy-scoped reading` `the second vacancy, with no Committee of its own`

§ `s 15 — Appointments to which the Act applies`

-- Royal Assent 2026-12-01; commencement 2026-12-02; 12 months on is 2027-12-02.
GIVEN made  IS A `Calendar date`
      start IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH AN `Appointment case`
`an unrecommended appointment of Blake made on` made `starting` start MEANS `Appointment case` WITH
    `the office`                                     IS `High Commissioner to India`
    `the appointee`                                  IS `Blake`
    `the day the appointment is made`                IS made
    `the day the term of the appointment starts`     IS start
    `the Selection Committees established for an appointment to the office` IS EMPTY
    `the days of earlier appointments to the office` IS EMPTY
    `the Minister is satisfied the appointee does not have a significant political affiliation` IS FALSE
    `both Houses have passed a resolution approving the appointment` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`an unrecommended appointment of Blake made on` (`the date` 2027 6 1) `starting` (`the date` 2027 9 1)) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `this Act does not apply to the appointment (s 15)`
#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`an unrecommended appointment of Blake made on` (`the date` 2027 6 1) `starting` (`the date` 2027 12 1)) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `this Act does not apply to the appointment (s 15)`
#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`an unrecommended appointment of Blake made on` (`the date` 2027 6 1) `starting` (`the date` 2027 12 2)) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `the appointment must not be made (s 14(1)); if made it is valid (s 14(2)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(3))`
-- Made the day before commencement, for a term starting years later: outside the Act.
#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`an unrecommended appointment of Blake made on` (`the date` 2026 12 1) `starting` (`the date` 2030 1 1)) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `this Act does not apply to the appointment (s 15)`
-- s 7: an office that is not designated.
#ASSERT `the status of the appointment in` (`Appointment case` WITH `the office` IS `another office of the Commonwealth` "Ambassador to France" TRUE FALSE, `the appointee` IS `Blake`, `the day the appointment is made` IS `the date` 2028 1 1, `the day the term of the appointment starts` IS `the date` 2028 2 1, `the Selection Committees established for an appointment to the office` IS EMPTY, `the days of earlier appointments to the office` IS EMPTY, `the Minister is satisfied the appointee does not have a significant political affiliation` IS FALSE, `both Houses have passed a resolution approving the appointment` IS FALSE) `given Royal Assent on` `the day of Royal Assent` EQUALS `the office is not a designated diplomatic office (s 7), so this Act does not govern the appointment`

§ `s 11 — Acting arrangements`

GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH AN `Acting arrangement`
`an acting arrangement for` p MEANS `Acting arrangement` WITH
    `the office`                      IS `High Commissioner to Canada`
    `the chargé d'affaires`           IS p
    `the day the arrangement is made` IS `the test day`
    `the occasion`                    IS `a vacancy in the office`

#ASSERT `the status of the acting arrangement` (`an acting arrangement for` `Avery`) EQUALS `the arrangement may be made (s 11)`
#ASSERT `the status of the acting arrangement` (`an acting arrangement for` `Blake`) EQUALS `the arrangement must not be made (s 14(4)); if made it is valid (s 14(5)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(6))`
#ASSERT `the status of the acting arrangement` (`an acting arrangement for` `Casey`) EQUALS `the arrangement must not be made (s 14(4)); if made it is valid (s 14(5)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(6))`
#ASSERT `the status of the acting arrangement` (`an acting arrangement for` `Quinn`) EQUALS `the arrangement must not be made (s 14(4)); if made it is valid (s 14(5)) but must be terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister becomes aware (s 14(6))`

